{"title":"Career Roadmap · Yoga Therapist","role":"Yoga Therapist","summary":"A Yoga Therapist uses structured, individualized yoga-based practices as part of a broader health and wellness plan. A BNYS graduate brings additional knowledge of naturopathy, anatomy, physiology, pathology, lifestyle management and therapeutic yoga.","facts":{"Current degree":"BNYS (Naturopathy & Yogic Sciences)","Course":"Naturopathy & Yoga"},"about":[],"intro":[],"horizons":[],"sections":[{"heading":"Career Overview","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"A Yoga Therapist uses structured, individualized yoga-based practices as part of a broader health and wellness plan. A BNYS graduate brings additional knowledge of naturopathy, anatomy, physiology, pathology, lifestyle management and therapeutic yoga."},{"type":"h","text":"The role may involve:"},{"type":"h","text":"Individual yoga-therapy assessment"},{"type":"h","text":"Therapeutic yoga session planning"},{"type":"h","text":"Breathing practices"},{"type":"h","text":"Relaxation techniques"},{"type":"h","text":"Meditation practices"},{"type":"h","text":"Mobility and flexibility work"},{"type":"h","text":"Posture and movement correction"},{"type":"h","text":"Lifestyle counselling"},{"type":"h","text":"Stress-management programs"},{"type":"h","text":"Preventive-health education"},{"type":"h","text":"Group therapeutic sessions"},{"type":"h","text":"Wellness program design"},{"type":"h","text":"Progress monitoring"},{"type":"h","text":"Collaboration with doctors and other healthcare professionals"},{"type":"h","text":"Community and institutional wellness programs"},{"type":"p","text":"A professional Yoga Therapist should distinguish therapeutic yoga and wellness support from medical diagnosis and treatment and operate within the applicable professional scope and institutional protocols."}]},{"heading":"Career Pathway","kind":"growth","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"Class 12 — PCB"},{"type":"h","text":"BNYS"},{"type":"flow","items":["F